666
00:34:04,290 --> 00:34:08,190
但一旦前额叶皮层决定要惩罚某人，
But once the prefrontal cortex decides to punish,

667
00:34:08,300 --> 00:34:11,320
脑的另一部分决定了惩罚程度--
another part of the brain decides how much --

668
00:34:11,430 --> 00:34:14,290
这就是负责我们情感的杏仁体。
the amygdala, which governs our emotions.

669
00:34:14,400 --> 00:34:17,130
惩罚的决定是两个
The punishment decision is a product

670
00:34:17,240 --> 00:34:19,460
完全不同区域的产物--
of two very different regions --

671
00:34:19,570 --> 00:34:21,130
一个分析高度理性，
one highly analytic,

672
00:34:21,240 --> 00:34:25,270
一个更为感性的决定惩罚的量--
one more emotional that is setting a punishment amount --

673
00:34:25,380 --> 00:34:29,400
这两部分独立地存在，但对于如何决定惩罚
that are separately deployed but yet jointly involved

674
00:34:29,520 --> 00:34:32,380
又相互联系在一起。
in yielding the punishment decision.

675
00:34:32,490 --> 00:34:37,210
脑部情感与理性分析的部分的平衡作用，
Balancing the emotional and analytic parts of the brain

676
00:34:37,330 --> 00:34:41,250
是每个法官和陪审人员需要的神奇技巧，
is the magic trick required of every judge and jury.

677
00:34:41,370 --> 00:34:44,890
如果陪审团脑中这两部分的任何一个功能降低，
If jurors have reduced function in either area,

678
00:34:45,000 --> 00:34:48,330
他们的惩罚决定就有瑕疵。
their punishment decisions could be flawed.

679
00:34:48,440 --> 00:34:51,230
类似这样的研究也许会使
Research like this may enable us

680
00:34:51,340 --> 00:34:52,760
我们的决定不再偏颇，
to de-bias decisions

681
00:34:52,880 --> 00:34:56,500
使我们在给人定罪时
really focused on those aspects of a person's behavior

682
00:34:56,610 --> 00:34:59,340
尽量聚焦于考虑人类行为的
that we want to take most into account

683
00:34:59,450 --> 00:35:02,040
多个方面。
when setting degrees of culpability.

684
00:35:02,150 --> 00:35:04,270
Owen希望他的发现
Owen hopes his findings

685
00:35:04,390 --> 00:35:07,210
最终可以使定罪更为公平--
will eventually lead to fairer sentencing --

686
00:35:07,320 --> 00:35:10,210
最终使我们的司法体系
that we will eventually have a legal system

687
00:35:10,330 --> 00:35:12,010
只把那些真正想害人的人
that only imprisons people

688
00:35:12,130 --> 00:35:14,650
投入监狱...
who truly want to do harm to others...

689
00:35:14,760 --> 00:35:18,650
而不是那些意外造成悲剧结果的人。
rather than those who simply made tragic errors.

690
00:35:18,770 --> 00:35:22,590
但即使我们断定罪犯的方式进步了，
But even if we improve the way we judge criminals,

691
00:35:22,710 --> 00:35:27,200
我们还是无法进入消除邪恶的最后阶段。
it will not be the endgame in the struggle to eliminate evil.

692
00:35:27,310 --> 00:35:31,170
因为，历史见证，
Because, as history bears witness,

693
00:35:31,280 --> 00:35:36,740
有时候，整个社会都会失去它的道德指南，
sometimes entire societies lose their moral compass.

694
00:35:36,850 --> 00:35:40,690
我们如何才能消除邪恶所毒害所有的国家？
How do we stop the evil that poisons whole nations?

695
00:35:43,390 --> 00:35:48,160
我们知道邪恶会扭曲个体思维，
We know that evil can twist and bend solitary minds,

696
00:35:49,040 --> 00:35:53,470
但是有另一种邪恶的形式会感染全社会，
but there's another form of evil that infects whole societies.

697
00:35:53,580 --> 00:35:58,510
它迫使普通人支持种族灭绝政权
It compels ordinary people to support genocidal regimes

698
00:35:58,620 --> 00:36:02,350
和以奴隶制为基础的经济。
and economies based on slavery.

699
00:36:02,460 --> 00:36:05,080
是什么使社会都变坏了？
What makes societies turn bad?

700
00:36:05,190 --> 00:36:08,420
我们能否阻止这样的情况发生？
Can we stop it from happening?

701
00:36:08,530 --> 00:36:11,220
Karen Wynn在耶鲁大学做的实验
Karen Wynn's experiments at Yale

702
00:36:11,330 --> 00:36:15,220
表明即使婴儿也能分辨正义和邪恶
show that even babies have a sense of good and evil

703
00:36:15,340 --> 00:36:17,530
而且还倾向于正义与善良。
and seem to prefer goodness.

704
00:36:17,640 --> 00:36:20,400
但Karen做了另一个
But Karen runs another experiment

705
00:36:20,510 --> 00:36:22,660
让人不怎么舒服的实验。
that is far less comforting.

706
00:36:22,780 --> 00:36:27,740
结果表明人类从很小的时候就
It shows that the human tendency to identify with groups

707
00:36:27,850 --> 00:36:30,970
倾向于建立组群，
and discriminate against those not in "our" group

708
00:36:31,090 --> 00:36:33,440
歧视团体以外的人。
starts very young.

709
00:36:33,560 --> 00:36:34,610
这项研究中，
In this study,

710
00:36:34,720 --> 00:36:37,610
我们在婴儿前面放两种食物以供选择--
we present the baby with two food choices --

711
00:36:37,730 --> 00:36:40,320
全麦饼干，和青豆。
graham crackers and, say, green beans.

712
00:36:40,430 --> 00:36:43,190
接下来，我们把孩子带到实验室中，
Then, we bring babies into our experimental room,

713
00:36:43,300 --> 00:36:45,490
向他们展示两个玩偶，
and they're introduced to two puppets.

714
00:36:57,110 --> 00:37:01,500
哟！呸！我不喜欢全麦饼干。
Ew! Yuck! I don't like graham crackers.

715
00:38:15,420 --> 00:38:18,110
或是是否有一样的肤色，
or have the same color skin.

716
00:38:33,770 --> 00:38:37,160
Steve Pinker是哈佛的一位实验心理学家
Steve Pinker is an experimental psychologist

717
00:38:37,280 --> 00:38:39,700
和认知科学家。
and cognitive scientist at Harvard.

718
00:38:39,810 --> 00:38:42,900
历史上许多最严重的暴行
A lot of the worst atrocities in history

719
00:38:43,020 --> 00:38:44,640
都随着一部分人的人性丧失
came about when one group

720
00:38:44,750 --> 00:38:47,010
或妖魔化另一部分人产生。
dehumanized or demonized another.

721
00:38:47,120 --> 00:38:49,510
他们会觉得这另一部分人是次等人类，
They may have thought that they were subhuman,

722
00:38:49,620 --> 00:38:52,340
就像害虫、老鼠或蟑螂。
that they were like vermin, like rats or cockroaches.

723
00:38:52,460 --> 00:38:54,280
许多道德进步会都随着
A lot of moral progress might come

724
00:38:54,390 --> 00:38:55,750
我们改变自己的心态产生，
when we change our mind-set,

725
00:38:55,860 --> 00:38:58,050
不再把人分为不同的群体，
and instead of dividing people into groups,

726
00:38:58,160 --> 00:39:00,220
而是想成同一种类，
think of the species as a group.

727
00:39:00,330 --> 00:39:03,220
把世界看成一个大村子，
Think of the world as being one big village

728
00:39:03,340 --> 00:39:05,560
每个人都是我们部落的一部分。
and everyone is part of our tribe.

729
00:39:05,670 --> 00:39:09,030
Steve认为这种思考方式的改变，
Steve thinks this change in thinking,

730
00:39:09,140 --> 00:39:11,760
从认同小团体
from identifying with small groups

731
00:39:11,880 --> 00:39:16,070
到属于一个包容一切的社会正在缓慢发生。
to belonging to one inclusive society, is slowly happening.

732
00:39:16,180 --> 00:39:20,710
最明显的效应就是暴力事件的急剧下降，
The most obvious effect has been a dramatic decline in violence.

733
00:39:20,820 --> 00:39:23,810
当我告诉人们暴力已经在
When I tell people that violence has been in decline

734
00:39:23,920 --> 00:39:25,150
很长一段时间内减少了，
for long stretches of time

735
00:39:25,260 --> 00:39:28,350
我们可能生活在人类历史上
and that we're probably living in the most peaceful era

736
00:39:28,460 --> 00:39:31,320
最安宁的时期的时候，他们都认为我是个疯子。
in the history of our species, they think I'm nuts.

737
00:39:31,430 --> 00:39:34,860
这就需要我通过写一本800页厚的书，
So I had to make the case with a book that was 800 pages long,

738
00:39:34,970 --> 00:39:38,460
一张又一张图，一组又一组数据，
with graph after graph and statistic after statistic,

739
00:39:38,570 --> 00:39:41,070
来向人们证明我的观点。
just to prove the point to people.

740
00:39:46,480 --> 00:39:48,000
比如说，距离我站的地方不远处，
For example, not far from where I'm standing,

741
00:39:48,120 --> 00:39:49,470
就是波士顿的一个区域，
there's an area of Boston

742
00:39:49,590 --> 00:39:51,840
过去曾被称作“战区”，
that used to be called the "Combat Zone"

743
00:39:51,950 --> 00:39:53,880
因为那里非常多的凶杀、
because there were so many murders

744
00:39:53,990 --> 00:39:55,440
刺伤与抢劫事件，
and stabbings and muggings.

745
00:39:55,560 --> 00:39:58,610
现在那里被年轻的都市自由职业者占据。
Now it's being re-colonized by young urban professionals.

746
00:39:58,730 --> 00:40:01,720
或许几百年前，据这里不远处
Or a few hundred years ago, there were wars going on,

747
00:40:01,830 --> 00:40:03,150
更是战斗频发，
not far from here,

748
00:40:03,260 --> 00:40:06,250
加拿大、英国和法国在此争战。
that involved enemies like Canada and Britain and France.

749
00:40:06,370 --> 00:40:08,820
现在说起这些国家之间发生战争
Now the idea of a war with those countries

750
00:40:08,940 --> 00:40:10,400
听起来就像开个不好的玩笑。
would seem like a bad joke.

751
00:40:10,520 --> 00:40:11,520
300年前，
300 years ago,

752
00:40:11,630 --> 00:40:13,430
我可能就被绑在桩子上烧死，
I might have been burned at the stake

753
00:40:13,540 --> 00:40:15,030
因为我持着像今日的这些信念，
for beliefs that I hold today,

754
00:40:15,140 --> 00:40:16,700
再往前一百年，
and a hundred years before that,

755
00:40:16,810 --> 00:40:19,240
我可能就在印第安战争中
I might have had my head cut off with a hatchet

756
00:40:19,350 --> 00:40:20,370
被战斧砍掉了脑袋。
in the Indian wars.

757
00:40:20,480 --> 00:40:23,170
很难把人类历史上的
It is difficult to overstate

758
00:40:23,290 --> 00:40:26,140
暴力和残忍程度
just how violent and cruel the world was

759
00:40:26,260 --> 00:40:29,280
再描述得更加夸张了。
for much of the history of the human race.

760
00:40:29,390 --> 00:40:33,580
曾经奴隶制在全世界都是合法的，
Once, slavery was legal everywhere in the world.

761
00:40:33,700 --> 00:40:38,220
现在全球已经正式认定其违法性质。
Now it is officially illegal everywhere in the world.

762
00:40:38,340 --> 00:40:41,260
战争和凶杀曾是日常发生的事实，
War and murder were daily facts of life.

763
00:40:41,370 --> 00:40:44,960
现在对于大多数人来说，这些都是特殊事件。
Now, for most people, they are exceptional events.

764
00:40:45,080 --> 00:40:47,770
Steve将这种改变归于
Steve attributes most of this change

765
00:40:47,880 --> 00:40:51,570
政府和法律功能的增强，
to the increased role of government and the rule of law.

766
00:40:51,680 --> 00:40:52,970
但他同时也认为，
But he also thinks

767
00:40:53,080 --> 00:40:56,270
现在的人类比祖先更聪敏。
people today are sharper than their ancestors.

768
00:40:56,390 --> 00:40:57,710
你也许会想，
You might wonder,

769
00:40:57,820 --> 00:41:00,880
人们变得更好是因为更聪明了么？
are people getting nicer because they're getting smarter?

770
00:41:00,990 --> 00:41:03,620
不论你是否相信，答案也许是这样的。
And, believe it or not, the answer is, maybe yes.

771
00:41:03,730 --> 00:41:07,790
全世界人类的IQ值在整个20世纪
I.Q. scores have been increasing throughout the 20th Century

772
00:41:07,900 --> 00:41:09,490
持续增加。
and all over the world.

773
00:41:09,600 --> 00:41:11,320
没有人知道为什么，
No one knows exactly why,

774
00:41:11,440 --> 00:41:15,190
但有可能是结合了教育的增加
but it's probably a combination of increased schooling

775
00:41:15,310 --> 00:41:17,960
与从科学渗透到日常生活中的
and a trickle down of technological

776
00:41:18,080 --> 00:41:21,900
科技和分析的观念造成的。
and analytic concepts from science into everyday life.

777
00:41:22,010 --> 00:41:25,270
不过作为结果，我们自然会想到
But, as a result, it's not farfetched to think

778
00:41:25,380 --> 00:41:28,770
比起刚开始理智生活的人类，
that people could see the benefits of cooperation

779
00:41:28,890 --> 00:41:31,640
人们更会通过合作寻找利益，
and see the downsides of violence more

780
00:41:31,760 --> 00:41:34,980
更会看到暴力的缺点。
as they start to intellectualize their lives.

781
00:41:35,090 --> 00:41:39,080
大量的交流与运输，
Mass communication and mass transportation

782
00:41:39,200 --> 00:41:42,590
打破了我们之间的屏障，
are breaking down the barriers between us,

783
00:41:42,700 --> 00:41:45,560
同样也增加了我们对
and so is our increasing knowledge

784
00:41:45,670 --> 00:41:47,860
人类思维的工作原理的知识。
of how the human mind works.

785
00:41:47,970 --> 00:41:52,730
我们学的越多，越能看清我们的人性，
The more we learn, the more we see the humanity within us all,

786
00:41:52,850 --> 00:41:55,350
包括我们认为是邪恶的。
even those we think of as evil.

787
00:41:58,320 --> 00:42:03,810
没有邪恶踪影的世界仍是一个幻想，
A world without a trace of evil will remain a fantasy,

788
00:42:03,920 --> 00:42:07,250
但是随着我们对大脑的了解，
but the better we understand the brain,

789
00:42:07,360 --> 00:42:09,520
我们就能更好的
the better able we are to identify

790
00:42:09,630 --> 00:42:11,650
甄别出我们之中危险的想法，
the most dangerous among us

791
00:42:11,770 --> 00:42:15,260
并在其造成危害之前制止。
and stop them before they do serious harm.

792
00:42:15,370 --> 00:42:17,690
我们也许无法消除邪恶，
We may never eliminate evil,

793
00:42:17,800 --> 00:42:21,200
或许我们能够将其包容，
but perhaps we can contain it

794
00:42:21,310 --> 00:42:25,010
降低我们生活中的损失。
and reduce the damage it does to our lives.

